# This project is LF everywhere -- in the repository and in the working tree,
# on every platform.
#
# The reason is the test corpus, not taste.  tests/expected/ and
# tests/expected_run/ are compared byte for byte against output the compiler
# writes with '\n', so a checkout that converts them to CRLF makes every golden
# file fail on the platform it was converted for.  The shell runners need LF
# for the same reason they always did, and MSVC, MinGW, GCC and Clang all read
# LF source without complaint -- so there is nothing left to vary per platform.
#
# text=auto lets Git detect binary content and leave it alone; eol=lf pins the
# working-tree ending for everything it decides is text.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Test fixtures are exact bytes: never detected, never normalised, never
# translated.  A single byte changed here is the whole point of the file.
*.cxb binary
